{"overview":"In Renaissance Florence, a Florentine trader meets a shipwrecked stranger, who introduces himself as Tito Melema, a young Italianate-Greek scholar. Tito becomes acquainted with several other Florentines, including Nello the barber and a young girl named Tessa. He is also introduced to a blind scholar named Bardo de' Bardi, and his daughter Romola. As Tito becomes settled in Florence, assisting Bardo with classical studies, he falls in love with Romola.","cast":[{"n":"Lillian Gish","c":"Romola","p":"/xUBj1vajDHS8GntuBzhpztRMVy4.jpg","q":"Q104183"},{"n":"Dorothy Gish","c":"Tessa","p":"/pawOaoP0uk1NZ5vDLizFohzx6Tn.jpg","q":"Q234536"},{"n":"William Powell","c":"Tito Melema","p":"/8DTWs389THkVCTiDFu0x8ekNmUC.jpg","q":"Q105960"},{"n":"Ronald Colman","c":"Carlo Bucellini","p":"/2Rw0UG4QLk8cDCTGZZ5RxFK1e41.jpg","q":"Q181786"},{"n":"Charles Lane","c":"Baldassar Calvo","p":"/vpIxv89AjguuVgaXaHRTWYpALwD.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Herbert Grimwood","c":"Savonarola","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Bonaventura Ibáñez","c":"Bardo Bardi","p":null,"q":"Q3642047"},{"n":"Frank Puglia","c":"Adolfo Spini","p":"/r1wLNTEnjKEQGrfUB5qzf8RpiCn.jpg","q":"Q283123"},{"n":"Amelia Summerville","c":"Brigida","p":"/jxbyyifaBJ5vU3NQFXHwxVztKiB.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Tina Ceccaci Renaldi","c":"Monna Ghita","p":null,"q":null}],"country":["United States"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romola_(film)","qid":"Q3441247","rel":{"US":{"d":"1924-12-06","c":"NR"}},"backdrops":["/ynNXbh6gO8u6ZuY8yVKpsqzlMOy.jpg","/uiPqj0pssj06vJ9MhVQkcLulewk.jpg","/79oXG8jvolhJnTQghf7KtUBwse8.jpg","/3D1WT71axksPbraWkTlsIoiXF5i.jpg","/5BH7we78gGFZdPtzfaZiBhEoW9Z.jpg","/sc1efwrYpii36Voll0F16eHxbM3.jpg","/v5LvsNMnJsgKZthSKa01rW3Lk1P.jpg","/f73FwNvg75hozxcaixuGDtf202I.jpg"]}